    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- The points logic lives in the `Owner` domain model, exactly where the old `getMembershipLevel()` already lived \u2014 the right unit, and consistent with the other derived-property accessors nearby (`getIdentityKey()`, `getCheckDigit()`).\n- Good separation into two single-responsibility methods: `getMembershipPoints()` computes the score, `getMembershipLevel()` does only the points\u2192level banding. No logic is duplicated, and the level mapping reads clearly.\n- The `OwnerMapper.addMembershipLevel` `@AfterMapping` hook is extended additively to also copy `membershipPoints`, matching the existing pattern of pulling domain-computed values onto the DTO; its Javadoc was updated accordingly.\n- The OpenAPI schema was updated in step (new `membershipPoints`, revised `membershipLevel` description and `maximum: 4`), keeping the contract in sync.\n- Field access (`this.householdSize`) matches the surrounding in-class style even though the Javadoc references `getHouseholdSize()`; consistent with how other methods in this class read fields directly.\n\nA maintainer would find this natural.",
